{"name": "Kogilicious", "address": "956 Embarcadero Del Norte", "city": "Isla Vista", "state": "CA", "categories": "Korean, Restaurants", "hours": {"Monday": "10:0-23:0", "Tuesday": "10:0-23:0", "Wednesday": "10:0-23:0", "Thursday": "10:0-23:0", "Friday": "10:0-23:0", "Saturday": "10:0-23:0", "Sunday": "10:0-23:0"}, "attributes": {"BusinessParking": {"garage": false, "street": true, "validated": false, "lot": false, "valet": false}, "RestaurantsReservations": false, "OutdoorSeating": true, "WiFi": "no", "RestaurantsTakeOut": true, "RestaurantsGoodForGroups": true, "Music": null, "Ambience": {"romantic": false, "intimate": false, "touristy": false, "hipster": false, "divey": false, "classy": false, "trendy": false, "upscale": false, "casual": true}}, "business_stars": 4.0, "review_info": [{"review_stars": 5.0, "review_date": "2015-12-31 04:01:57", "review_text": "Half and half beef ribs and pork FTW.  Best I've *ever* had, and I've had a lot of good Korean food."}, {"review_stars": 5.0, "review_date": "2015-08-31 01:14:22", "review_text": "So. Good. So good. A Kogilicious spicy chicken burrito is one of my favorite foods in the world. But all of the proteins are fantastic- beef, spicy pork, tofu; can't go wrong. Taco, burrito, both are great. And so reasonably priced! Pay cash; you'll get a giant burrito for less than $7, which is unheard of elsewhere in IV. This town desperately needs a proper Korean restaurant, but in the meantime, Kogilicious hits the spot."}, {"review_stars": 4.0, "review_date": "2015-07-22 23:44:51", "review_text": "Three words, Spicy Pork Burrito.

Bomb.

Bring cash, they charge more if you use a card."}]}

{"name": "Montecito Confections", "address": "1150 Coast Village Rd, Ste E", "city": "Montecito", "state": "CA", "categories": "Restaurants, Bakeries, Food", "hours": {"Monday": "9:0-17:0", "Tuesday": "9:0-17:0", "Wednesday": "9:0-17:0", "Thursday": "9:0-17:0", "Friday": "9:0-17:0"}, "attributes": {"BusinessParking": {"garage": false, "street": true, "validated": false, "lot": false, "valet": false}, "RestaurantsReservations": null, "OutdoorSeating": null, "WiFi": null, "RestaurantsTakeOut": null, "RestaurantsGoodForGroups": null, "Music": null, "Ambience": null}, "business_stars": 4.5, "review_info": [{"review_stars": 5.0, "review_date": "2014-08-14 04:36:40", "review_text": "Ordered a white cake with buttercream. When I placed the order they suggested a light lemon cream filling which I went with. It was beyond perfect. Light fluffy buttercream, moist cake, and the filling was a perfect match up. Yep, I will be back!"}, {"review_stars": 5.0, "review_date": "2014-08-07 19:34:34", "review_text": "Katie baked the wedding cake of my dreams. It came out exactly as I wanted and was delicious. We had three tiers: two were red velvet and one was vanilla custard cake with fresh raspberries. I am very happy with our decision to choose her."}, {"review_stars": 5.0, "review_date": "2014-05-09 15:00:38", "review_text": "Katie Teall is an ANGEL!!!  I made a wedding cake for the daughter of a very close High School friend and the Fondant I bought (FondArt) was horrible.  I spent about 7 hours kneading it and rolling it, and no matter what I did when I covered a tier of the cake it cracked.  I was so stressed that decided to go to Montecito Confections to see if I could buy Fondant there.  I got there and asked Katie Teall the sweet adorable, British owner if she could help me.  she explained that she sold the store and the rest of her Fondant was for the last 15 wedding cakes that she had to deliver during the summer.  She must have seen my face of stress, exhaustion, just lost, and asked:  How big is your cake?  I told her and she said:  Do you want me to cover it in Fondant for you?  I jumped to hug her and kiss her and hug her and kissed her some more.

I came home and the mother of the bride carried the bottom tier and we went back to Montecito Confections to be saved by Katie.  We arrived and she said where is the rest of the cake?  I did not want to take advantage so we just took the biggest tier.  She said:  Bring it!

Home we went after hugging Katie and kissing her some more and got help and left with two more tiers.  Katie my angel covered the three tiers!!! She was my angel.  The mother of the bride broke in tears, I guess she was worried that I was never going to serve the wedding cake.  These were tears of relief!  We ended up having the most beautiful cake and thanks to Katie.  Katie also build the cake, putting all three tiers together.  Then explained to me how to decorate it.  She told me to get a photo of the container of her fondant because she had tried all the different brands and that was the best of them all.  She said that mine was impossible to work with since it was too dry!  Katie is a walking ANGEL.  I love her, love her and love her.  All the kisses and hugs are not enough to thank her for saving the wedding cake and so much more."}]}

{"name": "Brasil Arts Cafe", "address": "1230 State St, Ste C", "city": "Santa Barbara", "state": "CA", "categories": "Juice Bars & Smoothies, Breakfast & Brunch, Brazilian, Restaurants, Food, Salad, Acai Bowls", "hours": {"Monday": "17:0-20:30", "Thursday": "17:0-20:30", "Friday": "17:0-20:30", "Saturday": "10:0-21:0", "Sunday": "10:0-16:0"}, "attributes": {"BusinessParking": {"garage": false, "street": true, "validated": false, "lot": false, "valet": false}, "RestaurantsReservations": true, "OutdoorSeating": true, "WiFi": "free", "RestaurantsTakeOut": true, "RestaurantsGoodForGroups": true, "Music": null, "Ambience": {"touristy": false, "hipster": false, "romantic": false, "divey": false, "intimate": false, "trendy": false, "upscale": false, "classy": true, "casual": true}}, "business_stars": 4.0, "review_info": [{"review_stars": 5.0, "review_date": "2021-12-21 06:50:22", "review_text": "Our hosts Roberta and Mestre Daniel Yoshimi (aka Prof. Chin) provided an excellent menu of the favorite foods of Brazil (o Brasil, em português). One who appreciates tasty-good food simply cannot stay away very long. My tri tip was delicious, and the multiple traditional sides were exactly on-point. (Prices are friendly too.)

I used to visit this establishment weekly to take part in great African drumming classes, and it's fun to revisit the festive atmosphere and food. They present their cuisine and culture with hospitality, nuance and great cooking skills.

#HighlyRecommended"}, {"review_stars": 5.0, "review_date": "2021-12-18 05:28:16", "review_text": "my boyfriend and I went here for dinner and it was a nice experience :) we each got a caipirinha to drink which was good and my boyfriend LOVED the stroganoff! My Brazilian cesar was good and the brigadiero which we got to go was AMAZING! I would go back to try more! The lady told us to make ourselves at home which was a sweet sentiment!! The people were very nice :,)"}, {"review_stars": 4.0, "review_date": "2021-12-15 12:06:28", "review_text": "The restaurant facility itself may not look all that elegant and appealing but the service and the food really blows that away. They serve food for each meal of the day but I personally would recommend going for breakfast and trying one of their acai fruit bowls. Slightly on the pricier side but so worth it and you will be healthily full for hours to come! The culture here is also something that is unique and interesting. Great place for family brunch!"}]}

{"name": "Peebee & Jays", "address": "1007 Casitas Pass Rd", "city": "Carpinteria", "state": "CA", "categories": "Sandwiches, Restaurants", "hours": {"Monday": "10:30-16:0", "Tuesday": "10:30-16:0", "Wednesday": "10:30-16:0", "Thursday": "10:30-16:0", "Friday": "10:30-16:0", "Saturday": "10:30-16:0"}, "attributes": {"BusinessParking": {"garage": false, "street": false, "validated": false, "lot": true, "valet": false}, "RestaurantsReservations": false, "OutdoorSeating": true, "WiFi": "no", "RestaurantsTakeOut": true, "RestaurantsGoodForGroups": false, "Music": null, "Ambience": {"romantic": false, "intimate": false, "touristy": false, "hipster": false, "divey": false, "classy": false, "trendy": false, "upscale": false, "casual": true}}, "business_stars": 4.0, "review_info": [{"review_stars": 4.0, "review_date": "2021-10-21 19:40:04", "review_text": "Their sandwiches are fantastic, but don't opt for the cauliflower flatbread. They pack so much into these sandwiches that the flatbread can't handle it, so you're paying extra for a flimsier sandwich. I've also had trouble getting all my points for my weekly purchases. Their system is confusing, and they were unresponsive after multiple attempts to fix it. That said, their sandwiches are all great. Go for soft rolls with the Bacon Went on a Date and add turkey. So good."}, {"review_stars": 4.0, "review_date": "2021-10-14 20:09:15", "review_text": "I got a lot pb with honey and a Nutella pb with marshmallow fluff they were pretty good the only real issue I had was that the crust was rubbery and hard to but into but over all it was super delicious"}, {"review_stars": 1.0, "review_date": "2021-10-13 20:20:58", "review_text": "I will never go back to this location again. The workers in general have a negative attitude and think the customers owe them a medal for showing up to work. I placed a pick up order and put on the special instructions for the Mayo and Mustard to be on the side. Well, I got my sandwich and it was drenched in Mayo, something I wanted to avoid. I called them and the employee told me they could remake it. I threw the sandwich away and about 15 mins later got a call and was told that I had to bring the sandwich back. I told them I already tossed it in the garbage then the employee put his manager on the line and she was so RUDE and said that I need to bring it back ( I wasn't about to dig through the trash) and I said that the employee never said anything about bringing the sandwich back in the first conversation and he should have said something and expect me to still have it. And she said very unprofessionally, "well he didn't know." I told her that is a failure on the training and not the customer. She then said that next time I need to specifically write the word "everything" on the side instead of using commas as I did. This manager is absolutely disgusting and clearly has no basic customer service skills. 

This isn't the first time my pick up order has been destroyed. But the way that "manager" spoke to me and handledis why I will NEVER go there again and will tell all my coworkers to stay away. 

To the owner of this location: good Managers are hard to come by but you can absolutely do better then who was working on 10/13/21 @ 12:30 pm. She is horrible at her job and will continue to drive away customers with her terrible attitude."}]}
